full_article:
Cockroach Janta Party (CJP) founder Abhijeet Dipke said comparisons of the Jantar Mantar protest against the NEET exam paper leak with the uprisings in Bangladesh and Nepal were being made to "defame" the outfit.

"Protests in Bangladesh and Nepal are being used to defame us. We are different," Abhijeet Dipke said, responding to remarks made by exiled Bangladeshi writer Taslima Nasreen on the CJP protest during an interview with PTI.

She said on Sunday that while she had not followed the CJP protest in India, a clip of it reminded her of the 2024 student uprising in Bangladesh, which led to the ouster of then Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina.

