"It was like that. That student movement in Bangladesh fooled us. Because we thought the students wanted to abolish the quota system. Sheikh Hasina had also agreed to their demands, but ultimately the government fell. Later, we found that jihadis were behind that movement. The fallout has not been good for Bangladesh," Nasreen was quoted as saying by PTI.

The CJP held a 36-day protest at Jantar Mantar in Delhi against the paper leak that led to the resignation of Dharmendra Pradhan as education minister last month.

